--- !u!114 &2029595964
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2029595962}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 0
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "HARDCORE TRUCK CHEESE ROLLING\nCHASE THE CHEESE\nStarting slots shuffle
    across the full sixteen-position grid, including the outside. Trees have breakable
    physical roots: trucks and exploding sheep can knock them fully down, and fallen
    trunks stay collidable. Rocks, cats, wolves and tall-grass patches change each
    round, with clear routes preserved. Only the marked, colored participants can
    score. Twelve background racers create chaos but never earn or consume points.
    First genuine truck-body contact earns one catch. First to five wins. Solo is
    a timed five-catch challenge. There is no finish-line score.\n\nCONTROLS\nYour
    assigned keyboard cluster or stick steers and accelerates. Opposite throttle
    brakes before reversing. Whole controller: left stick steer, RT forward, LT reverse;
    Y/North recovers. Esc / assigned Start pauses. Each player can RECOVER from the
    pause screen, including shared-stick players. Airborne input gives a small bounded
    correction. Momentum remains live while tumbling or damaged.\n\nWEATHER AND HAZARDS\nClear,
    blizzard, and hurricane conditions rotate with the round seed. Snow lowers grip;
    rain makes the runout slick; everyone feels the same gusts. Cheese stays indestructible.
    Actual sheep have explosive red collars. Truck contact triggers a powerful broad
    blast, temporary damage and nearby chain reactions. Steer around them or risk
    a spectacular launch.\n\nFAIR CATCHES\nDramatic 3 / 2 / 1 / GO: begin accelerating
    while 2 is displayed, then hold through GO for a jump boost. Pressing early or
    late does not qualify; releasing cancels it. AI obeys the same timing rule. The
    cheese gets a short head start during 1. Background contact never stops scoring.
    Contacts from different participants in the same physics step cause a neutral
    replay with unchanged scores. Cheese escaping or genuinely unreachable also replays
    neutrally. Low-speed mud chases remain live.\n\nRECOVERY\nRecovery uses a safe
    nearby point at or behind prior progress, at least nine metres behind the cheese,
    avoiding trucks and blast sites. It clears dangerous motion, has a five-second
    cooldown, and requires separation before scoring. Damage reduces control briefly
    without stopping flight or sliding.\n\nSETUP AND PAUSE\nOne to four participants,
    any human/AI combination, independent difficulties. Names, sources and colors
    persist through rematches. Whole controllers have one owner; independent left/right
    sticks can share one pad. Disconnect pauses the entire race without losing bodies,
    scores or weather. Assign replacement explicitly and release controls before
    resuming. The mushroom look reuses Taxi's world-wave shader and vivid grading
    with a sport-owned sky. Pause \u2192 MUSHROOM LOOK cycles full / low / off. It
    never affects physics or the HUD. No networking, collectible powerups, cancellation
    scoring or permanent elimination."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
